EasyPrescription is a web application that allows users (patients) to submit their medical prescriptions and associate them with a pre-selected pharmacy. The project simulates the prescription submission workflow and does not handle real or sensitive medical data.

This application was developed during the Coding Weeks Hackathon as a team project.

Features:

I. User authentication
- User account creation (patients only)
- Login and logout

II. Prescription submission
- Upload of a prescription image (no image processing applied)
- Selection of a pharmacy from a pre-defined list stored in the database

III. User dashboard
- Display of submitted prescriptions with their status (e.g. 'Pending')
- Ability to delete a submitted prescription

Not implemented in the current version : 

- Pharmacy interface: pharmacies are pre-registered in the database, but they cannot actively manage prescriptions (e.g. mark them as "prepared" or "completed").

Tech Stack : 

- Backend: Python, Django
- Database: SQL
- Frontend: HTML, CSS
- Authentication: Django built-in authentication system

